{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 13 — Functional tools: itertools, functools, map/filter, lambda\n","Objectives:\n","- Use itertools for iterables.\n","- functools.lru_cache and partial.\n","- When to prefer vectorization over map/filter in DS code."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import itertools as it\n","from functools import lru_cache, partial\n","\n","list(it.accumulate([1,2,3,4]))\n","\n","@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n","def fib(n:int)->int:\n","    return n if n<2 else fib(n-1)+fib(n-2)\n","\n","fib(30)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Use groupby to group pairs by key.\n","2) Use partial to create a specialized function from a generic one.\n"]}]}
